      "note_id": "borrowed_words",
      "kind": "helpful_transfer",
      "text": "English and Indonesian are not related, but they have lent each other words, so you already know some. The first group are English words that came from Malay, the language Indonesian grew out of, or from Javanese, sometimes by way of Dutch or Portuguese (ketchup may have come this way too, from Chinese by way of Malay). The last group went the other way: Indonesian borrowed them from Dutch or English, and English has the same Latin and Greek roots, so they look alike.",
      "pairs": [
